Fabric authorization lookup failures
===================================

Fabric permission checks reject missing, inactive, soft-deleted and foreign-org
authors. A permission check is not enough to authorize an unrestricted site
scope: the following grant lookup must also succeed.

For a stored actor ID, resolve_actor_site_grants now refuses an unavailable,
inactive, deleted or missing author instead of returning an unrestricted scope.
Database/client exceptions produce a fixed PermissionError without exposing the
original exception details through caller logs or execution history. Both native
automation fabric.operation actions and Fabric Connection steps stop before the
operation executor when this lookup fails.

Successfully resolved org administrators remain unrestricted by site grants.
The existing hybrid model also preserves an unrestricted scope for an active
user with zero configured site grants. Missing actor IDs remain neutral only
for explicitly permission-free native operations; protected operations must
reject missing identity at their permission gate.

This closes error and missing-author fallbacks. It does not add transaction-wide
authorization fencing, make an in-flight external effect revocable, or establish
exactly-once event execution. Other Fabric concerns, including shared event-claim
and cooldown outages and per-site permission ceilings, need separate evidence.
